    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Vinnie Pasquantino** (76.21) serving as our primary anchor. His matchup against Arrighetti is our most favorable environment, bolstered by an 18% SP skill boost and a dynamic platoon advantage that elevates him into elite territory. We are also heavily leaning into the speed-first profile of **Corbin Carroll** (73.35) and **Mickey Moniak** (73.14). While **Mickey Moniak** faces a slightly tougher hurdle with Leahy\u2019s 3.94 xERA, his massive 14% park factor boost and favorable spot in the order make him an essential play. **James Wood** (67.15) remains a high-upside start; despite the \"Lineup Pending\" status, his elite 0.417 xwOBA and the base-stealing potential against a slower pitcher make him a cornerstone for our pursuit of the stolen base category.\n\nThe most difficult benching decision of the day involved **Josh Naylor** (56.73). He trailed **Travis Bazzana** (56.33) and **Isaac Paredes** (58.54) by a razor-thin margin, but the optimizer ultimately faded him due to a unfavorable park factor and a platoon disadvantage against Jump. **Austin Riley** (57.08) snuck into the utility spot despite a bottom-third order placement, as his 8% BvP historical edge against Nola provided just enough mathematical weight to keep him ahead of the bench. We are tracking a minor risk with **James Wood** and **Josh Naylor** due to the unconfirmed lineups, and we remain cautious regarding **Griffin Conine** (48.97); his limited score reflects the suppressed ceiling against Holmes, though his inclusion is necessary to maximize our volume in a tight Roto race. **Trevor Story** (70.35) presents a unique case; despite an elite hold SP warning that suppresses his stolen base floor, his 16% park advantage keeps his efficiency score well within our strong start range.",
